diff --git a/changes/4404.feature.md b/changes/4404.feature.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..cfa685ed
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/4404.feature.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Reading data encoded with the `pickle` codec now requires an explicit opt-in, because unpickling data from an untrusted store can execute arbitrary code ([GHSA-jqc8-qjfv-5m6r](https://github.com/zarr-developers/numcodecs/security/advisories/GHSA-jqc8-qjfv-5m6r)). Enable it with `zarr.config.set({"array.allow_unsafe_pickle_decode": True})` or the environment variable `ZARR_ARRAY__ALLOW_UNSAFE_PICKLE_DECODE=True`. Without the opt-in, reading such data raises `zarr.errors.PickleCodecDisabledError`. numcodecs has its own opt-in (`numcodecs.pickles.ALLOW_UNSAFE_PICKLE_DECODE`), which must also be enabled. Writing with the `pickle` codec is unchanged.
diff --git a/changes/4539.bugfix.md b/changes/4539.bugfix.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..62f2472e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/4539.bugfix.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+The minimum supported numcodecs version is now 0.16.6, and 0.17.0 is excluded. Those versions leave `Pickle.decode` enabled by default, which allows arbitrary code execution when reading an untrusted Zarr v2 array ([GHSA-jqc8-qjfv-5m6r](https://github.com/zarr-developers/numcodecs/security/advisories/GHSA-jqc8-qjfv-5m6r)).
diff --git a/docs/user-guide/config.md b/docs/user-guide/config.md
index d1a70a14..a97feb85 100644
--- a/docs/user-guide/config.md
+++ b/docs/user-guide/config.md
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ Configuration options include the following:
 - Whether empty chunks are written to storage `array.write_empty_chunks`
 - Enable experimental rectilinear chunks `array.rectilinear_chunks`
 - Whether missing chunks are filled with the array's fill value on read `array.read_missing_chunks` (default `True`). Set to `False` to raise a [`ChunkNotFoundError`][zarr.errors.ChunkNotFoundError] instead.
+- Whether data encoded with the `pickle` codec can be read `array.allow_unsafe_pickle_decode` (default `False`). Unpickling can execute arbitrary code, so only enable this for data from a source you trust, e.g. with `zarr.config.set({'array.allow_unsafe_pickle_decode': True})` or the environment variable `ZARR_ARRAY__ALLOW_UNSAFE_PICKLE_DECODE=True`. While it is disabled, reading such data raises a [`PickleCodecDisabledError`][zarr.errors.PickleCodecDisabledError]. Writing with the `pickle` codec is not affected. numcodecs has a separate opt-in for the same reason (`numcodecs.pickles.ALLOW_UNSAFE_PICKLE_DECODE = True`, or `NUMCODECS_ALLOW_UNSAFE_PICKLE_DECODE=1` before importing numcodecs); both must be enabled to read pickled data.
 - Async and threading options, e.g. `async.concurrency` and `threading.max_workers`
 - Selections of implementations of codecs, codec pipelines and buffers
 - Enabling GPU support with `zarr.config.enable_gpu()`. See [GPU support](gpu.md) for more.
